<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 604 0 R/Alt(Two line plots side by side against r, a mode's amplitude over its reference amplitude, from 0 to 2.5. Left panel, frequency change in percent: two orange curves with circle and square markers, the member's mode at about 111 Hz, rise from zero as a parabola and level off at their caps, the strong size higher; two blue curves with triangle and diamond markers, an article mode at about 264 Hz, fall in a straight line to r = 1 and then stay flat, the strong size deeper. Right panel, damping over its small-signal value: all four curves rise in a straight line to r = 1 and then stay flat, the article mode reaching higher than the member mode and the strong size higher than the realistic.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[93]/Pg 1963 0 R>>
endobj
