<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 635 0 R/Alt(Three panels. Left, a side-view line drawing: two hatched clamp posts stand on a chassis tube 50 mm apart, a thin strip spans between them, and a gray block 20 mm long and 20.7 mm tall sits on the strip at mid-span, with a double arrow showing its up-and-down motion. Middle, a plan-view drawing: two parallel strips, each 7.5 mm wide and 50 mm long, 51.2 mm apart, each clamped by hatched posts at both ends, with a gray rectangular mass of 166 grams of steel, 20 by 51.2 mm, spanning both strips at mid-span. Right, a line plot of frequency rise in percent against RMS motion of the mass from 0 to 0.2 mm: a blue solid curve with circles for the realistic strips rises as a parabola to 1 percent at about 0.08 mm and 6 percent at 0.2 mm; an orange dashed curve with squares for the strong strips rises four times as fast, to 4 percent at about 0.08 mm; a dash-dot vertical line at 0.081 mm marks the stated motion and dotted horizontal lines mark 1 and 4 percent.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 1965 0 R>>
endobj
