1431 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 1432 0 R/Alt(Four panels in a two by two grid, sharing a vertical axis of change in decibels from 0 to about 4.5. In each panel three groups sit along the horizontal axis: control gauges, held-out gauges and stress. Each group has three markers with error bars: blue open circles joined by a solid line for softening joints only, orange open triangles joined by a dashed line for the hardening member only, and gray open squares joined by a dotted line for both; beside each open marker a filled marker of the same shape and color gives the held-back structures. In nearly every panel the stress group is highest. The orange triangles lie lowest throughout, below the blue circles. Panel (a), realistic size with twelve control gauges, has every value under about 0.5 dB. Panels (b) and (c) reach about 1 to 1.2 dB at stress. Panel (d), strong size with six control gauges, is highest: stress about 1.9 dB for softening, 0.7 for hardening and 2.4 for both, with the control gauges at about 1 dB for softening and both.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 1978 0 R>>
endobj
